<title>UK: German inland gas oil eases, demand sluggish.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil eases, demand sluggish.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.6237)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     40.30/40.70     24.81/25.06     40.40/40.80</p>
<p> BREMEN		40.30/40.70     24.81/25.06     40.40/40.80</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    40.30/40.70     24.81/25.06     40.70/41.10</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   41.60/42.00     25.62/25.86     41.70/42.10</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   41.40/41.80     25.49/25.74     41.70/42.10</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  43.10/43.50     26.54/26.79     43.30/43.70</p>
<p>German inland gas oil eased 20 pfennigs on Monday. Consumer demand was sluggish, and traded volumes were low. Ice problems continue in parts of the Mosel and Elbe regions, resulting in movements by rail. -- London newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
</text>
